This is Part II of a series about vertical partitioning for large text columns. Part I explains why we separated the large text from the main table. In Part I, we split one books table into two tables: CREATE TABLE books ( id BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY, title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL, author VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL, isbn VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL, published_year SMALLINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL );
CREATE TABLE book_contents ( book_id BIGINT UNSIGNED PRIMARY KEY, resume TEXT NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY (book_id) REFERENCES books(id) ON DELETE CASCADE );
